    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49278": {
      "title": "Pre-School Teacher",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Pre-School Teacher Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Pre-School Teacher Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Pre-School Teacher Posting Number NFE03159P Department USD-Head Start Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text USD Head Start is seeking a passionate and dedicated Center Teacher to join our preschool team in Vermillion, SD. In this role, you’ll guide a classroom of 16 children ages 3–5, helping them build the social, emotional, and early academic skills that set the foundation for lifelong learning. What You’ll Do Lead a preschool classroom of 16 children Create a nurturing, developmentally appropriate learning environment Support each child’s growth through engaging activities and individualized attention Build strong relationships with families and collaborate with a supportive team Position Details Full‑time, 40 hours per week 9.5‑month schedule (August 15 – May 31) Located in Tea, South Dakota Eligible for the full State of South Dakota benefits package Qualifications BA in Early Childhood Education, Education with Early Childhood Endorsement,Special Education with Early Childhood specialization Experience working with young children Benefits This position includes the comprehensive State of South Dakota benefits package: Health insurance Paid annual and sick leave Paid holidays Matching contributions to the South Dakota Retirement System ( SDRS ) Posting Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 08/18/2026 Advertised Salary commensurate with qualifications, plus benefits Duration of the Term 9.5 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Work Hours This position is a 9.5 month, 100% time in Vermillion. Working hours 7:45 a.m. to 4:15 p.m. with 1/2 hr. unpaid lunch break. Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Faculty Status No Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Other If other, please indicate Passing Fingerprint background check Department Description and Cultural Expectations Head Start provides free health, education and development services to families with young children. A federally funded program, we work with families to recognize their unique characteristics, cultural values and strengths, and offer services like: - Individualized learning - Vision, hearing and developmental screenings - Nutritious meals and snacks - Health services - Parent education - Community resource information We offer services in Clay, Lincoln, Turner and Union counties. These services are available in-home or at one of our local centers and some are offered on a full-day, year-round basis. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement USD is committed to fostering a dynamic and welcoming working and learning environment for all. USD provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to ideological, political, or sectarian opinions or perspectives; or race, color, creed, religion, sex, ancestry, disability, national origin, or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. USD is committed to the principles of free expression and encourages the timely and rational discussion of topics in an environment that is intellectually and ideologically diverse. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Comprehend, Frequent Change, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Multiple Stimuli, Pace-fast, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. Latex Gloves, Protective Clothing If other protection is used please identify N/A Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Balancing, Bending, Stooping, Twisting, Crouching, Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting light, Pushing/Pulling, Reaching, Squatting, Stretching, Use Both Hands, Use of Either Hand, Independently, Walking Describe any of the conditions selected Position must be able to engage and supervise children ages 3-5 in multiple learning environments. Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Depth Perception, Distant Vision, Hearing, Near Vision, Peripheral Vision, Speaking, Vision (With and without corrective lenses), Color Vision Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Biohazard, Exposure or Potential Exposure to Blood/Body Fluids, Extreme Weather Conditions (wind, rain, snow, humidity), Vaccination recommended due to potential occupational exposure, Exposure to Infectious Diseases, Walking/Standing on rough or uneven surfaces (gravel, rocks, etc) Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Exposure to common childhood illnesses and supervision of children in indoor and outdoor environments; assist children with toileting as needed; care of injuries to children. Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Classroom Environment, Other Environment (Please explain below) If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. The majority of time is in the classroom; but position does do in-home visits with students. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Reference List Optional Documents Other The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
