    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49655": {
      "title": "Accountant",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Accountant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Accountant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Accountant Posting Number CSA02817P Department USD-Accounting Services Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text USD is seeking an energetic, creative problem solver, and strategic thinker to fill an open Accountant position. The individual hired must be able to interpret, analyze, and determine accuracy of financial data in the maintenance of controlling funds. Individual must be able to provide exceptional customer service and interpret USD and State of SD policies and procedures. Specific tasks will include: Audit direct pays and journal vouchers. Process and track state contracts Plan and Provide traning on Banner accounting processes campus wide Manage data interface transactions into Banner and review for accuracy Manage 1099 process Reconcile accounts and disburse payment Candidates must demonstrate: - Extensive knowledge of accounting principles and practices - Ability to interpreting complex policies and regulations - Ability to work effectively with a variety of units to create effective relationships for problem solving and positive interactions - Ability to use computers and software for detailed accounting and budgeting transactions - Ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and electronically. - Ability to work with staff whose understanding of financial operations will be at various levels This position is not eligible for sponsorship, all eligible candidates must be authorized to work in the United States. Posting Date 09/03/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 09/10/2026 Advertised Salary Starting rate is $23.56; based on qualifications and internal equi