    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48303": {
      "title": "Health Sciences Faculty--QE8767",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Health Sciences Faculty--QE8767 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Health Sciences Faculty--QE8767 Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Health Sciences Faculty--QE8767 Posting Number F01886P Department USD-Health Sciences Major Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text The University of South Dakota Department of Public Health and Health Sciences, within the School of Health Sciences, invites applications for an instructor or lecturer position. This faculty position offers an exceptional opportunity to work with a dedicated team of faculty and staff to prepare graduates for a wide variety of health careers. This is a continuing faculty role structured on a 9-month contract. The faculty member will be responsible for classroom instruction and online instruction in the following undergraduate education content areas: interprofessional health teams, health career exploration, and the influences of culture, policy, and literacy on health. Applicants must hold a graduate degree and have undergraduate and/or graduate preparation in health, education, or human services, or a combination of relevant academic preparation and professional experience; an MPH is preferred. Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position. Posting Date 05/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 06/28/2026 Advertised Salary Duration of the Term 9 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Tenure Status Term Proposed Rank Work Hours Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search Department Description and Cultural Expectations Equal Employment Opportunity Statemen