    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/46910": {
      "title": "Instructional Designer",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Instructional Designer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Instructional Designer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/1225/docs/115824.png Institution Northern State University Working Title Instructional Designer Posting Number NFE02966P Department NSU-Graduate School Physical Location of Position (City) Aberdeen Posting Text Position Summary: Northern State University seeks a collaborative faculty-support professional to lead instructional design initiatives and coordinate Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning ( CETL ) operations in support of continuous improvement in teaching and learning. A key priority is helping NSU faculty leverage Northern’s unique e-learning mission to enhance teaching and learning across all modalities, including on campus, online, and HyFlex. Key Responsibilities: * Faculty Support & Instructional Design • Guide course development and improvement across all modalities (on campus, online, and HyFlex) using best practices in instructional and universal design. • Lead the Quality Assurance Review process for online and HyFlex courses. • Consult with faculty on course design, technology integration, experiential learning, and digital tools. • Ensure compliance with accreditation standards and federal regulations in coordination with Online Learning and Continuing Education. Leadership in Pedagogy • Champion experiential learning and support faculty in adopting new technologies, expanding student engagement, and redesigning assessments to support student learning outcomes. • Design and deliver trainings, including creating micro-credentials for online and HyFlex instruction. • Share research in teaching and learning, assessment, teaching innovations, and student success through CETL communications and strategic initiatives. CETL Program Coordination • Manage CETL events, trainings, communications, and day-to-day operations. • Supervise CETL graduate assistant and technology fellow. Represent NSU in SDBOR and COPLAC teaching networks and coordinate faculty mentoring efforts. Knowledge of : * Pedagogy, learning management systems, learning theories, technologies and computer software. Skill & Ability to: Communicate effectively, maintain confidentiality, collaborate across faculty of various ranks and disciplines, prioritize daily tasks while advancing long-term goals, host events and trainings, organize an office and manage student employees, and maintain detailed records. Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree required. Master’s degree preferred. Degree in instructional design, technology, pedagogy, education, preferred. Posting Date 02/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 02/18/2026 Advertised Salary DOE Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Work Hours 8-5. Typical Hours Worked Per Week 40 Appointment Type Regular Faculty Status No Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Travel, Overnight stays If other, please indicate Department Description and Cultural Expectations Northern State University seeks a collaborative faculty-support professional to lead instructional design initiatives and coordinate Center for Excellence in Teaching and Learning ( CETL ) operations in support of continuous improvement in teaching and learning. Key Responsibilities: Faculty Support & Instructional Design Guide course development and improvement across all modalities (on campus, online, and HyFlex) using best practices in instructional and universal design. Lead the Quality Assurance Review process for online and HyFlex courses. Consult with faculty on course design, AI integration, experiential learning, and digital tools. Ensure compliance with accreditation standards and federal regulations in coordination with Online Learning and Continuing Education. Leadership in Pedagogy Champion experiential learning and support faculty in adopting new technologies, expanding student engagement, and redesigning assessments to support student learning outcomes. Design and deliver trainings, including creating micro-credents for online and HyFlex instruction. Share research in teaching and learning, assessment, teaching innovations, and student success through CETL communications and strategic initiatives. CETL Program Coordination Manage CETL events, trainings, communications, and day-to-day operations. Supervise CETL graduate assistant and technology fellow. Represent NSU in SDBOR and COPLAC teaching networks and coordinate faculty mentoring efforts. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of: Pedagogy Learning management systems Learning theories Technologies and Computer Software Skill & Ability to: Communicate effectively Maintain confidentiality Collaborate across faculty of various ranks and disciplines Prioritize daily tasks while advancing long-term goals Host events and trainings Organize an office and manage student employees Maintain detailed records Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Northern State University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or protected veteran status. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Pace-average, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. If other 