    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49428": {
      "title": "IT Engineer",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | IT Engineer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help IT Engineer Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title IT Engineer Posting Number CSA02794P Department USD-VP for Admin & Technology Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text USD is seeking an IT Engineer to provide support to install, program, test, and maintain infrastructure systems at the University of South Dakota. The successful candidate will support hardware and software needs for the campus, work with vendors to specify hardware and software solutions and recommend enhancements to campus infrastructure and resources. This position includes on-call responsibilities. This is a 100% full time position, on campus in Vermillion, SD. Duties include working with a variety of network services, security systems, email services, directory services, configuration management products, storage systems, virtualization products, cloud services, load balancing systems, and web systems. Responsible for: Daily service requests, break/fix work Ensuring clear documentation is created and maintained for all infrastructure services Monitoring performance and availability of infrastructure systems Accurate inventory maintenance Documenting test plans and their outcomes Knowledge of: Networking protocols and operating systems Client and server operating systems (Windows, Mac OS, Linux) Cloud infrastructure and services (Azure Cloud, Microsoft 365) Storage systems and data backup systems Systems and Network operating Center monitoring tools Security Technologies Ability to: Troubleshoot and repair IT infrastructure problems Identify and implement improvements to IT infrastructure Communicate technical concepts to non-technical users Communicate effectively both orally and in writing Evaluate new hardware and software for usefulness and to determine the best solution to needs Establish and maintain effective working relationships with fellow employees, clients, and vendors Work effectively as a team member Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position Posting Date 08/17/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 08/31/2026 Advertised Salary Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Work Hours 8 – 5 Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Travel, Weekends/Holidays, Valid Drivers License If other, please indicate Department Description and Cultural Expectations Equal Employment Opportunity Statement USD is committed to fostering a dynamic and welcoming working and learning environment for all. USD provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to ideological, political, or sectarian opinions or perspectives; or race, color, creed, religion, sex, ancestry, disability, national origin or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. USD is committed to the principles of free expression and encourages the timely and rational discussion of topics in an environment that is intellectually and ideologically diverse. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Frequent Change, Logic, Memory, Pace-average, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. If other protection is used please identify Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requiremen