    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49601": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Admissions Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Admissions Counselor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Admissions Counselor Posting Number NFE03187P Department USD-Admissions Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text The University of South Dakota Office of Admissions is seeking an energetic, goal-oriented, self-motivated individual for the position of Admissions Counselor. Responsibilities include, territory management, marketing and recruitment activities on and off campus, assist in financial aid as necessary, database management, counseling prospective students and families, contributing to overall enrollment management goals, evaluating prospective students and participating in the selection of applicants for admission. Qualifications: Bachelors degree and valid driver’s license required. Related admissions experience preferred. Knowledge of The University of South Dakota campus, departments, and admission standards desirable. Ideal candidates will have excellent communication skills (both oral and written), be self-starters, and have the ability to be creative in developing recruiting opportunities, and be proficient in Microsoft Office. This position is not eligible for sponsorship. Applicants must be eligible to work in the United States. Posting Date 08/31/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 09/14/2026 Advertised Salary commensurate with qualifications Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Work Hours Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Faculty Status No Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Travel, Overnight stays, Weekends