    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49523": {
      "title": "MBM Pillar 3 Director",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | MBM Pillar 3 Director Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help MBM Pillar 3 Director Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title MBM Pillar 3 Director Posting Number T00286P Department SSOM - Medical Education Physical Location of Position (City) Sioux Falls Posting Text The University of South Dakota Sanford School of Medicine is seeking a dedicated individual to be the Pillar 3 Director. This position coordinates curriculum and guides students in their academic programs. Pillar 3 occupies the final sixteen months of medical school when students complete required clerkships (sub-internship, emergency medicine, surgery sub-specialties, rural family medicine), electives, and interview for residencies. These clerkships may be located at Rapid City, Sioux Falls, or Yankton, as well as at out-of-state or international locations. POSITION SUMMARY : The Pillar 3 Director coordinates curriculum and guides students in their academic programs. 1. Develop, implement and maintain high-quality curricula in Pillar 3 to expand clinical learning opportunities, and to provide training in important and emerging areas, e.g., preparation for residency, Quality/Safety. (40%) Develop and implement new curriculum in Pillar 3 to expand opportunities for students Mentor faculty in required Pillar 3 courses, e.g. sub-internships and in the development of electives Bring new course proposals to the Medical Education Committee Explore options to offer distinction opportunities including micro credentialing and certificates Lead development of the Medical Accelerated Program in partnership with the residencies 2. Collaborate with the associate deans of medical education and medical student affairs and registration officer on Pillar 3 curricular programs. (30%) Collaborate in the implementation and maintenance of online Pillar 3 scheduling Develop and enforce policies for away electives Participate in sessions for Pillar 2 students on Pillar 3 course selection and preparation for residency application Run clinical competency committee meetings and track students on monitored academic status 3. Collaborate with the Office of Medical Education to assure programs meet accreditation requirements. (15%) Work with director of evaluation and assessment to monitor course requirements, evaluation data, timeliness of grades, and duty hours violations Provide regular reports to the Medical Education Committee and Clerkship Directors Committee Serve on the Medical Education Committee Integration Subcommittee Provide documentation when requested as part of continuous quality improvement for accreditation 4. Collaborate with clinical departments and clerkship directors in coordinating required clerkships and electives. (10%) Develop, implement, and oversee the processes of collecting student grades and reporting grades to the registrar in a timely manner Attend the clinical department assistants monthly meeting Attend the clerkship directors monthly meeting 5. Coordinate the Transition to Residency [ TTR ] course. (5%) Curriculum Development: Attend relevant conferences and symposia relevant to curriculum development in transition to residency Support specialty-specific curricular opportunities for students throughout the week Work with Parry Center to coordinate ‘Night on Call’ simulation experiences for students during Pillar 3 Review Program Director feedback on students’ residency preparedness to identify important themes to touch on during course Precepting: Precept small group and large group sessions the week of the course Coordinate daily paging simulation experience and debriefs Evaluation and Assessment: Identify mechanisms for giving students feedback on their readiness for residency Determine how students are assessed and assigning grades for the course Review student feedback on the TTR course and make changes as appropriate Communication/Coordination: Work with Pillar 3 assistant to recruit and schedule faculty for lecture and small group sessions (Morning Report, Journal Club) Develop relevant clinical skills sessions Coordinate sessions with faculty specialists in the area of Financial Wellness Qualifications: MD/DO with current SD Licensure or ability to obtain one and appropriate certification for field of specialty. Leadership experience in a medical school or similar environment. Experience in student services in an academic environment is preferable. This position reports to Dr. Amy Prunuske, PhD, Associate Dean of Medical Student Education. Posting Date 08/25/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 09/08/2026 Advertised Salary $77,000 .35 FTE Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent .35 Proposed Rank Work Hours Appointment Type Temporary This position requires Travel If other, please indicate Department Description and Cultural Expectations Equal Employment Opportunity Statement USD is committed to fostering a dynamic and welcoming working and learning environment for all. USD provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to ideological, political, or sectarian opinions or perspectives; or race, color, creed, religion, sex, ancestry, disability, national origin or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. USD is committed to the principles of free expression and encourages the timely and rational discussion of topics in an environment that is intellectually and ideologically diverse. Contact Information Amy Prunuske, PhD, Associate Dean for Medical Education amy.prunuske@usd.edu Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Multiple Priorities, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. If other protection is used please identify as needed/required by the clinic Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Driving, Fine Finger Manipulation (keyboarding, pipefitting, bench work, etc), Sitting for sustained periods of time, Standing for sustained periods of time Describe any of the conditions selected Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Clinical Environment If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Other Reference List The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
