    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48955": {
      "title": "Student Services Coordinator",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Student Services Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Student Services Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution Black Hills State University Working Title Student Services Coordinator Posting Number NFE03133P Department BHSU-Rapid City Campus Physical Location of Position (City) Rapid City Posting Text Black Hills State University is seeking applicants to fill a Student Services Coordinator. General Summary: Black Hills State University ( BHSU ) seeks a dynamic, student-focused professional to serve as the Student Services Coordinator at the BHSU–Rapid City campus. Reporting to the Vice President for Continuing Education & Workforce Development, this position serves as the primary front-facing representative of the university and plays a central role in recruitment, admissions, and enrollment services. The coordinator leads the student journey from initial inquiry through registration and transition to academic advising, ensuring a seamless and student-centered experience. This role is responsible for developing and executing strategic recruitment and outreach initiatives to support a broad range of student populations, including first-time/full-time students, adult learners, transfer students, and military-affiliated students (active duty, guardsmen, and veterans). The Student Services Coordinator also serves as the primary coordinator for BHSU–Rapid City events, leading the planning and execution of campus visits, preview days, recruitment events, and New Student Registration experiences. This position requires a highly motivated, self-directed professional who exercises independent judgment, thrives in a fast-paced environment, and is passionate about helping students succeed. Duties and Responsibilities: Recruitment & Enrollment Growth Lead strategic recruitment efforts to support enrollment growth across multiple student populations Develop partnerships with regional high schools, community colleges, workforce partners, and community organizations Coordinate and represent BHSU at recruitment events, community engagement activities, and outreach initiatives Develop targeted communication strategies and engagement plans to attract prospective students Analyze recruitment data and trends to inform strategy and improve outcomes Admissions & Enrollment Operations Review and evaluate admissions applications and supporting documentation Make informed admissions-related decisions in alignment with university policies Coordinate application processing workflows and ensure timely progression from application to admission Maintain accuracy and integrity of student data within institutional systems Resolve enrollment barriers using sound judgment and problem-solving Student Engagement & Enrollment Navigation Serve as the primary point of contact for prospective and incoming students (in-person, phone, and events) Lead students through the enrollment process from inquiry through registration Facilitate course registration when appropriate, including during peak periods and events Direct students to appropriate campus resources, ensuring smooth transitions to advising and other services Monitor student progression and intervene proactively to support completion of enrollment steps Financial Aid & Academic Pathway Support Provide front-line guidance on financial aid processes, including FAFSA completion Deliver general academic pathway information aligned with university programs Coordinate referrals to financial aid and advising specialists as needed Maintain working knowledge of financial aid processes, timelines, and requirements Student Services Coordination Lead coordination of student services across admissions, advising, and financial aid within the Rapid City location Facilitate regular team meetings and support cross-functional collaboration Coordinate service coverage, workflow alignment, and cross-training efforts Identify service gaps and implement improvements to enhance the student experience Strong ability to work independently and exercise sound judgment Excellent communication, presentation, and interpersonal skills Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment Strong customer service orientation and commitment to student success Ability to learn and apply complex policies and processes Events Coordination & Campus Experience Lead planning, coordination, and execution of BHSU–Rapid City events, including: Preview Days Campus visits and student tours Local recruitment events New Student Registration experiences Coordinate event logistics, communication, staffing, and materials Develop engaging, student-centered experiences that support recruitment and enrollment goals Evaluate event effectiveness and implement continuous improvements Communications & Social Media Engagement Coordinate and contribute to social media strategy for the Rapid City campus, including platforms such as Facebook and ZeeMee Develop and maintain engaging digital content aligned with institutional branding Support outreach campaigns through effective communication strategies and messaging Requirements Bachelor’s degree required One to three years of progressively responsible experience in admissions, student services, advising, enrollment management, or a related field Valid driver’s license required Ability to travel and work occasional evenings and weekends Preferred Qualifications Experience working with diverse student populations, including traditional-aged, adult, transfer, and military-affiliated students Experience in higher education recruitment, admissions, or student services Familiarity with student information systems such as Banner, DegreeWorks, or similar platforms Experience coordinating events or programs Demonstrated ability to build strong partnerships with community organizations and stakeholders COMMENTS Sponsorship is not available for this position. TO APPLY Applications must be made at http://yourfuture.sdbor.edu . Please attach a cover letter, resume, and the names and contact information of at least three professional references. This position is open until filled with a first review date of July 23, 2026 at 11:00 PM MDT . For application assistance, please contact Human Resources at 605.642.6549. Questions specific to the position may be directed to Ashley Armstrong at ashley.armstrong@bhsu.edu . Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting Cassie Maser at 605-642-6545 or Cassie.Maser@bhsu.edu . Employment is dependent upon a satisfactory background check. Posting Date 07/10/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 07/23/2026 Advertised Salary $20.29 depending on experience/qualifications Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Work Hours 8:00 am – 5:00 pm, Monday through Friday Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Faculty Status No Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Travel, Overnight stays, Weekends/Holidays, Valid Drivers License If other, please indicate Department Description and Cultural Expectations Black Hills State University is a masters-level state university with more than 3,300 students. The campus leads the region in sustainability efforts and maintains top academic programs in business ( AACSB Accredited), exercise science, natural sciences, social sciences, the arts, mass communication, health sciences and education. The University, founded in 1883, is located in the northern Black Hills, a region abundant with outdoor activity and culture. Spearfish, S.D., is recognized as one of the top 10 most livable small towns in the USA and has also been recognized nationally for outdoor recreational opportunities. A second location, BHSU -RC, is in Rapid City, the state’s second-largest city. BHSU , a member of NCAA Division II athletics, offers 14 sports, and has a legacy of champion rodeo teams. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Black Hills State University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Black Hills State University and the Board of Regents ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Intense Customer Interaction, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Multiple Stimuli, Pace-average, Perform calculations, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. If other protection is used please identify Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Driving, Sitting for sustained periods of time Describe any of the conditions selected Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Hearing, Speaking, Vision (With and without corrective lenses) Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Classroom Environment, Office Environment If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Where did you hear about this position? SDBOR Employment Site BHSU Website HigherEdJobs.com Chronicle of Higher Education SD Department of Labor Rapid City Journal Black Hills Pioneer Referral Other Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Reference List Optional Documents Transcripts Other The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
