    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48346": {
      "title": "Research Assistant Professor",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Research Assistant Professor - Chemistry Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Research Assistant Professor - Chemistry Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Research Assistant Professor - Chemistry Posting Number F01784P Department USD-Chemistry Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text The Chemistry Department of the University of South Dakota ( USD ) invites applicants to apply for a long-term Research Faculty position in chemistry related to modern refrigeration including but not limited to broadly defined fluorine chemistry. The initial appointment for this position will be at the Assistant Professor level. This hiring is in response to the R&D needs of newly established NSF Engineer Research Center: Environmentally Applied Refrigerant Technology Hub ( NSF ERC EARTH ), a large collaborative effort involving six academic institutions and fifteen industrial partners. A successful candidate is expected to bring in knowledge and skills that are align with the NSF ERC EARTH goals, and complementary to the expertise of current department faculty. The new research faculty is expected to provide guidance to graduate and undergraduate students, either through individual or collaborative effort with the department EARTH faculty. In addition to publication record, demonstrated ability to securing external funding is further thought to be an area of strength for a successful candidate. The position requires a PhD degree in chemistry, or closely related field, with preference given to candidate with postdoctoral experience or equivalent industrial working experience. Further questions regarding to the ERC EARTH program at USD campus, please reach out to the ERC EARTH’s USD lead person Dr. Haoran Sun at Haoran.Sun@usd.edu ; and questions regarding to the Chemistry Program, please reach out to the Department Chair Dr. James Hoefelmeyer at James.Hoefelmeyer@usd.edu . Interested applicants shall provide the following documents to the search committee through the SD BOR online job application portal: (1) cover letter, (2) CV, (3) detailed research plans (no more than 10 pages total including reference citation, with 1 inch margin around, single space, and font 11); (4) student mentoring plans (two page maximum, with 1 inch margin around, single space, and font 11); and (5) a list of contact information of three professional references. As the South Dakota’s flagship institution and one of the five core-partner institutions of the recently funded NSF ERC EARTH , the University of South Dakota provides vibrant study and working environment for its students and faculty. The Chemistry Department at USD offers BS and MS degrees in Chemistry and PhD degree in Materials Chemistry. Over the past twenty years, the Chemistry Program at USD receives very strong external funding support from federal, state, and industries including highly competitive NSF CAREER and NRT grants, and lately large collaborative NSF ERC grants. For more information about the Chemistry Department of the University of South Dakota, please go to the website at www.usd.edu/Academics/Colleges-and-Schools/college-of-arts-sciences/chemistry ; and about the ERC EARTH please go to the website at https://erc-earth.ku.edu . Posting Date 03/23/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 04/27/2026 Advertised Salary Duration of the Term 9 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Tenure Status Term Proposed Rank Assistant Professor Work Hours Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search Department Description and Cultural Expectations Equal Employment Opportunity Statement USD is committed to fostering a dynamic and welcoming working and learning environment for all. USD provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to ideological political or sectarian opinions or perspectives, or race, color, creed, religion, sex, ancestry, disability, national origin or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. USD is committed to the principles of free expression and encourages the timely and rational discussion of topics in an environment that is intellectually and ideologically diverse. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Frequent Change, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Multiple Stimuli, Pace-fast, Perform calculations, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. Eye Protection, Other If other protection is used please identify Laboratory personal protective equipment as needed to perform research safely. Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Fine Finger Manipulation (keyboarding, pipefitting, bench work, etc), Grasping, Lifting moderate, Pushing/Pulling, Reaching, Sitting for sustained periods of time, Standing for sustained periods of time, Stretching, Wrist Movement (twisting or rotating) Describe any of the conditions selected The candidate will operate within an office and laboratory space. The candidate will interface with computers, laboratory equipment and apparatus (including laboratory chemicals), and safety engineering controls. Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Depth Perception, Distant Vision, Hearing, Near Vision, Peripheral Vision, Speaking, Vision (With and without corrective lenses) Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Atmospheric Contaminants (includes odors & fumes), Chemical Hazards, Electrical Current, Extreme Cold, Extreme Heat >100F, Radiation Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Hazards include:  cryogens, laboratory chemicals, heating apparatus, electrical equipment, instrumentation that includes radiation generating devices such as X-ray diffractometer. Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Lab Environment, Office Environment If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Reference List Work or Writing Sample Optional Documents Portfolio Other The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49445": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President for Human Resources",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Associate Vice President for Human Resources Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Associate Vice President for Human Resources Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo https://pa-hrsuite-production.s3.amazonaws.com/1225/docs/115824.png Institution Northern State University Working Title Associate Vice President for Human Resources Posting Number NFE03162P Department NSU-Finance & Administration Physical Location of Position (City) Aberdeen Posting Text Northern State University invites applications for the position of Associate Vice President for Human Resources , an exceptional opportunity for an experienced human resources professional to serve as the University’s chief HR officer. Reporting to the Vice President for Finance and Administration and the Board of Regents Chief HR Officer, the Associate Vice President for Human Resources provides strategic leadership and operational oversight for all human resource functions while fostering a culture of excellence, engagement, and service across campus. In addition, this position serves as a valued member of the SD Board of Regents HR Leadership team. This position also provides comprehensive human resources and payroll services to the South Dakota School for the Blind and Visually Impaired, making it a unique opportunity to support two outstanding public institutions dedicated to education and student success. The Associate Vice President for Human Resources serves as a trusted advisor to executive leadership, managers, faculty, and staff on all aspects of human resources. This position is responsible for developing and implementing strategic HR initiatives that support the University’s mission and strategic plan while ensuring compliance with federal, state, and South Dakota Board of Regents policies. The successful candidate will lead initiatives in recruitment and retention, employee relations, performance management, compensation and classification, benefits administration, compliance, organizational development, payroll oversight, and HR information systems. Primary Responsibilities • Provide strategic leadership for all Human Resources operations. • Advise leadership on workforce planning, organizational development, and employee relations. • Lead recruitment, hiring, onboarding, and retention initiatives for faculty, staff, and administrators. • Oversee employee relations, workplace investigations, performance management, and corrective action processes. • Ensure compliance with employment laws and Board of Regents policies, including FLSA , FMLA , ADA , ACA , Title VII , Title IX, and EEO requirements. • Manage HR information systems, workforce reporting, and personnel records. Oversee payroll operations within a complex system governing Board of Regents campuses. • Support organizational effectiveness through strategic planning and data-informed decision-making. Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Management, Leadership, or a closely related field. • Significant progressively responsible professional experience in human resources, including management and leadership responsibilities. • Demonstrated knowledge of employee relations, employment law, compensation, benefits, recruitment, organizational development, and HR information systems. • Exceptional communication, interpersonal, analytical, and problem-solving skills. • Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and build collaborative relationships across the organization. Preferred Qualifications • Master’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Leadership, or a related field. • PHR , SPHR , SHRM -CP, or SHRM - SCP professional certification. • Experience working in higher education or another complex public-sector organization. Posting Date 08/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 08/24/2026 Advertised Salary Depends on Experience Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100% Work Hours 8-5 Typical Hours Worked Per Week 40+ Appointment Type Regular Faculty Status No Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Travel, Overnight stays, Valid Drivers License If other, please indicate Department Description and Cultural Expectations Northern State University is a student-centered public university committed to academic excellence, innovation, and community engagement. Located in Aberdeen, South Dakota, Northern offers a collaborative campus environment where employees make a meaningful impact on students, faculty, staff, and the communities we serve. We seek an experienced HR leader who is passionate about developing people, improving organizational effectiveness, and serving as a trusted partner to campus leadership. Position will report directly to the Vice President for Finance & Administration Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Northern State University is committed to building a welcoming culture of belonging and collegiality that respects diversity in knowledge, culture and world view. Northern seeks faculty and staff who will engage with individuals of diverse backgrounds, beliefs and perspectives to increase awareness, understanding, respect and opportunity for all. Must be authorized to work in the U.S. Sponsorship is not available for this position. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Frequent Change, Intense Customer Interaction, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Multiple Stimuli, Pace-average, Perform calculations, Reading, Reasoning, Verbal Communication, Written Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. If other protection is used please identify Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Fine Finger Manipulation (keyboarding, pipefitting, bench work, etc), Lifting light, Repetitive Motion, Sitting for sustained periods of time, Standing for sustained periods of time, Use Both Hands, Use of Either Hand, Independently, Walking, Wrist Movement (twisting or rotating) Describe any of the conditions selected Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Color Vision, Hearing, Near Vision, Speaking, Vision (With and without corrective lenses) Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Office Environment If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Reference List Optional Documents The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus Security & Crime Statistics Clery Report Position Definitions Notice to all applicants: If you are selected as a finalist, job references and a background check may be conducted. South Dakota Board of Regents 306 E. Capital Ave, Suite 200 Pierre, SD 57501 605-773-3455 Back to top Copyright © Faber To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
