    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48998": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business Analytics and Information Systems",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Assistant Professor of Business Analytics and Information Systems Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Business Analytics and Information Systems Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution Northern State University Working Title Assistant Professor of Business Analytics and Information Systems Posting Number F01926P Department NSU-Management Information Systems Physical Location of Position (City) Aberdeen Posting Text Northern State University’s School of Business is accepting applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Business Analytics. The successful candidate will support the School’s newly established Analytics major and contribute to the School’s existing Information Systems major. *Qualifications: Candidates holding a Ph.D. or D.B.A. in Business Analytics, Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Decision Sciences, Data Science, Computer Science, or a closely related field will be considered for a tenure-track appointment. Candidates from related quantitative business or technology fields may also be considered if their teaching and research background demonstrates expertise in analytics, information systems, business intelligence, data management, or applied technology. Applicants with a master’s degree in one of these areas will be considered for non-tenure-track positions. *Responsibilities: The successful candidate will be able to teach undergraduate information systems and analytics-related courses in both face-to-face and online settings. Potential teaching areas include management information systems, database management systems, business intelligence, systems analysis and design, data mining, and artificial intelligence in business. These courses support both the School’s newly established Analytics major and the existing Information Systems major. Depending on expertise, interest, and program needs, the successful candidate may have opportunities to develop additional analytics-related coursework, such as data visualization or other courses that support the continued growth of Northern’s School of Business. Additional responsibilities include academic advising and mentoring, scholarly activity, and service to the university, profession, and community. Posting Date 07/15/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 09/08/2026 Advertised Salary Depends on Experience Duration of the Term 9 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Tenure Status Tenure Track Proposed Rank Assistant Professor Work Hours 8-5 Typical Hours Worked Per Week 40 Appointment Type Regular Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search Department Description and Cultural Expectations Why Northern? Northern State University offers a supportive academic community where faculty are encouraged to innovate, collaborate, and make meaningful connections with students. Located in Aberdeen, South Dakota, Northern provides small class sizes, engaged students, and opportunities to contribute to a growing business program with strong ties to regional employers. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Northern State University is committed to building a welcoming culture of belonging and collegiality that respects diversity in knowledge, culture and world view. Northern seeks faculty and staff who will engage with individuals of diverse backgrounds, beliefs and perspectives to increase awareness, understanding, respect and opportunity for all. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Frequent Change, Intense Customer Interaction, Logic, Memory, Multiple Priorities, Multiple Stimuli, Pace-average, Perfor