    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/49157": {
      "title": "Accommodations Coordinator",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Accommodations Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Accommodations Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Accommodations Coordinator Posting Number NFE03150P Department USD-Office of Accessibility Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text The University of South Dakota is seeking an Accommodations Coordinator to join the Office of Accessibility. This role supports students registered with the university by coordinating reasonable and appropriate accommodations that allow full access to academic programs and services. Under the direction of the Director of Accessibility/504 Compliance, the successful candidate will be energetic, able to work with a team, and committed to helping students strengthen their self‑advocacy and self‑reliance as they work toward their academic and personal goals. Key Responsibilities Serve as the primary contact for students requesting accommodations. Review medical and psychological documentation to determine eligibility. Approve, coordinate, and monitor accommodation plans. Provide exam accommodations, including proctoring, scribing, or reading. Assist with accessible technology and accessible media needs. Maintain accurate case files and documentation. Work with faculty and staff to address accommodation needs and support classroom implementation. Provide case management and collaborate on process improvements. Supervise student workers who assist with accommodation delivery. Serve as a Campus Security Authority under the Clery Act. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution in a related or transferable discipline. 1–3 years of related experience. Strong communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of individuals. Ability to interpret documentation, manage multiple priorities, and maintain accuracy. Why This Role Matters Accommodation requests continue to grow each year, and timely coordination is essential to meeting institutional obligations and supporting student success. Posting Date 07/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 08/10/2026 Advertised Salary Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Work Hours 8 am to 5 pm during Spring and Fall, and 7:30a to 4:30p in the summer. Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Faculty Status No Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Travel, Valid Drivers License If other, please indicate Department Description and Cultural Expectations Equal Employment Opportunity Statement USD is committed to fostering a dynamic and welcoming working and learning environment for all. USD provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment without regard to ideological, political, or sectarian opinions or perspectives; or race, color, creed, religion, sex, ancestry, disability, national origin or any other factor protected by applicable federal, state, or local laws. USD is committed to the principles of free expression and encourages the timely and rational discussion of topics in an environment that is intellectually and ideologically diverse. Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Analyzing, Comprehend, Intense Customer Interaction, Memory, Pace-fast, Reading, Verbal Communication, Written Communication, Frequent Change, Multiple Priorities, Reasoning Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. If other protection is used please identify