    "https://yourfuture.sdbor.edu/postings/48867": {
      "title": "Custodial Operations Specialist",
      "description": "South Dakota Board of Regents Employment Opportunities | Custodial Operations Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Custodial Operations Specialist Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Logo Institution The University of South Dakota Working Title Custodial Operations Specialist Posting Number CSA02753P Department USD-Intercollegiate Athletics Physical Location of Position (City) Vermillion Posting Text Duties include: Performs routine event set-ups and custodial duties to ensure areas within the Athletic Department are prepared for both athletic and outside events and the facilities are well maintained. Must be able to work in a team environment with different individuals. This is a fast paced environment with a need for proactive attitude and good customer service skills. Must possess knowledge of light custodial and janitorial duties. Regular and reliable attendance is an expectation. Duties may include set-up and take-down of equipment for athletic and special events and may be required to move, lift, carry and/or arrange furniture, equipment, and other objects as needed. The duties also include but not limited to; clean and sanitize restrooms, collect and remove refuse from offices and buildings, dusting, mopping, window cleaning, carpet cleaning, waxing, scrubbing, polishing and snow removal from sidewalks and stairs. Qualifications: Ability to work at heights, and include but not limited to bending/stooping, pushing/pulling, balance, climbing, squatting/sitting, twisting, grasping, and crawling. Reach at various levels from floor to overhead. Ability to move/manipulate/carry up to 50 lbs. Posting Date 07/07/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes First Consideration Date 07/21/2026 Advertised Salary Duration of the Term 12 months If Other, describe duration Appointment Percent 100 Work Hours Depends on shift and event/game schedule. Typical Hours Worked Per Week Appointment Type Regular Scope of Search External (includes Internal) If internal, define scope of search This position requires Weekends/Holidays If other, please indicate Department Description and Cultural Expectations The University of South Dakota is the flagship institution of South Dakota, located on a 216-acre campus in Vermillion, in the southeast corner of South Dakota. USD is a NCAA Division I institution and a member of the Summit League and Missouri Valley Football Conference. For further information regarding USD , and the Athletic Department, please refer to our website at www.GoYotes.com. “Founded in 1862, The University of South Dakota is designated as the only public liberal arts university in the state and is home to a comprehensive College of Arts and Sciences, School of Education, School of Health Sciences, the state’s only School of Law, School of Medicine, the accredited Beacom School of Business and the College of Fine Arts. It has an enrollment of more than 10,100 students taught by 400 faculty members. More information is available at www.usd.edu/press/news.” Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Contact Information Working Conditions Cognitive Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the cognitive requirements for this position. Frequent Change, Pace-average, Verbal Communication Protective Clothing/Equipment Please check the appropriate response for this position's use of the following protective clothing or equipment. Ear Protection (including earplugs), Eye Protection, Latex Gloves, Protective Clothing, Surgical Mask If other protection is used please identify Physical Requirements Please designate the physical requirements of this position Balancing, Bending, Stooping, Twisting, Carrying, Climbing Ladders, Climbing Stairs, Crawling, Crouching, Driving, Fine Finger Manipulation (keyboarding, pipefitting, bench work, etc), Grasping, Kneeling, Lifting Above Waist, Lifting Below Waist, Lifting light, Lifting moderate, Lifting heavy, Pushing/Pulling, Reaching, Repetitive Motion, Squatting, Standing for sustained periods of time, Stretching, Use Both Hands, Use of Either Hand, Independently, Walking, Wrist Movement (twisting or rotating) Describe any of the conditions selected Sensory Requirements Please check the appropriate response that describe the sensory requirements for this position. Vision (With and without corrective lenses) Working Conditions & Exposures Working Conditions or Exposures (or potential exposures) that this position may encounter during the course of the work day. Walking/Standing on wood, metal or concrete, Changes of Temperature, Chemical Hazards, Exposure to Dust, Exposure to Noise, Extreme Weather Conditions (wind, rain, snow, humidity) Please describe, in more detail, any of the conditions checked above Working Environment Check the appropriate box(es) that best describes the environment in which the primary function of the position is performed. Athletic/Wellness Facilities If you have indicated Other Environment, if work tasks involve one or more of the above, or if further explanation is necessary, please use the space provided. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter Other Reference List The South Dakota Board of Regents is an Equal Opportunity Employer. The Board of Regents will take Affirmative Action to ensure that all employment practices are free of discrimination. In addition, the Board of Regents fully supports incorporation of non-discrimination and Affirmative Action rules and regulations into all of its employment practices. Arrangements for accommodations required by disabilities can be made by contacting the appropriate Human Resources office. Please see the Contact Us section of this webpage for more information. Veterans’ & Disability Preference/Re-employment Rights Campus